  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 3.12,
      "text": " This star could explode long after it has stopped shining."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.08,
      "end": 7.98,
      "text": " The trigger is not a growing mass. It is a falling limit."
    },
    {
      "start": 8.78,
      "end": 14.24,
      "text": " It's a black dwarf. The cold remnant, a white dwarf, could become in the far future."
    },
    {
      "start": 15.18,
      "end": 18.28,
      "text": " Inside, pressure from electrons resists gravity."
    },
    {
      "start": 19.42,
      "end": 25.68,
      "text": " In a theoretical model, quantum tunneling allows extremely slow fusion, gradually making"
    },
    {
      "start": 25.68,
      "end": 31.0,
      "text": " the core richer in iron. That changes how much mass the remnant can support."
    },
    {
      "start": 32.16,
      "end": 38.26,
      "text": " Its mass barely changes. Its limit falls. For some of the heaviest remnants,"
    },
    {
      "start": 38.94,
      "end": 44.08,
      "text": " gravity could finally win. Collapse. And a possible supernova."
    },
    {
      "start": 45.06,
      "end": 52.38,
      "text": " The earliest might wait 10 to the power of 1100 years. But only if protons don't decay first."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.38,
      "end": 56.8,
      "text": " A dead star with one more possible ending."
    }
  ]
}
